    "result_text": "All green \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`.\n\nThe audit log confirms the new format working end-to-end: `memberId=NSW2716E6609E1` = `NSW` (region) + `27` (FY 2027) + `16E6609E` (HASH8) + `1` (Luhn CHK).\n\n## Summary\n\nI unified `customerCode` + `membershipNumber` into a single `memberId` formatted `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>`, and removed the standalone `checkDigit`.\n\n**New / renamed function classes** (`rest/function/owner/`):\n- `MemberId.java` (replaces `CustomerCode.java`) \u2014 assembles `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>`: `of(region, fiscalYear, hash8)` appends the two-digit FY and a Luhn `CHK` over the digits of `<REGION><FY><HASH8>`; keeps `hash8(...)`; `region(memberId, knownRegions)` reads the region back by prefix match (no separators anymore).\n- `AssignMemberId.java` (replaces `AssignCustomerCode.java`) \u2014 computes region + FY (from `registrationDate`) + HASH8, and **collision handling now dedups on `memberId`** (`-<n>` suffix).\n- Deleted `MembershipNumber.java` and `CheckDigit.java`.\n\n**Referencing code updated to `memberId`:**\n- `Owner` model: field/column `customerCode`/`customer_code` \u2192 `memberId`/`member_id`; accessors `getMemberId`/`setMemberId`.\n- All four DB schemas: `customer_code` \u2192 `member_id` (bumped `VARCHAR(20)` \u2192 `VARCHAR(32)` to fit the `UNKNOWN`-region + dedup-suffix worst case).\n- `Locality` reads region from `memberId`; `Timezone` param renamed.\n- `AuditOwnerCreated` \u2014 audit line now carries `memberId` (dropped `membershipNumber`).\n- `OwnerCreatedEvent` \u2014 record field + JSON key `customerCode` \u2192 `memberId`.\n- `OwnerMapper` \u2014 dropped `membershipNumber`/`checkDigit` mappings; `memberId` auto-maps by name.\n- `owners.POST.yml` \u2014 step `customerCode` \u2192 `memberId` wired to `AssignMemberId`.\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 replaced the three schema properties with a single `memberId` (regenerates the DTO cleanly, no old fields).\n- Cleaned stale javadoc `{@link}`s in `Luhn`, `Sha256`, `FiscalYear`.\n\nThe `fiscalYear` response field, `MembershipPoints`, and `OwnerSegment` (via `Locality`) all continue to reference the fiscal year / region that now live inside `memberId`. The acceptance test (`coreReturnsUnifiedMemberId`) passes.",
